<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>Profit from a River Cruise</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02537</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Profit from a River Cruise</md:title>
    <md:uuid>f874d26b-eda3-4dd0-9515-54d8866f6ac9</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <para id="para-00001">A travel company uses a quadratic function to model the profit, in dollars, that it expects to earn from selling tickets to a river cruise at <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>d</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> dollars per person. The expression <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>d</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>100</m:mn><m:mi>d</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>900</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> defines this function.</para>
      <para id="para-00002">Without graphing, find the price that would generate the maximum profit. Then, determine that maximum profit.</para>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>
